# UC1 hand-graded evaluation stub dataset -- v0
# Authored by: tess (ML engineer, 2026-05-09)
# Status: STUB -- synthetic items for harness smoke-testing only.
#         Replace this file with Varn's 200-500 hand-graded scenarios when
#         they are delivered. The harness will read any JSONL matching the
#         HandGradedItem schema at the path passed to --dataset.
# Item count: 15
# Delta range covered: [-4.0, +4.5] (skewed positive to reflect competence bias
#   on matched legacy scenarios; full [-5,+5] coverage deferred to Varn's set).
#
# Grading rubric used for this stub:
#   +4 to +5  : character has deep matching legacy (20+ matched actions), ideal terrain
#   +2 to +3  : character has solid matching legacy (5-19 actions), decent terrain
#   +0 to +1  : weak match or neutral legacy
#   -1 to -2  : character has no matching legacy, moderate mismatch
#   -3 to -5  : strong mismatch (character trained for opposite environment/task)
# All prose is EN-pinned per encoder lock 2026-05-05.
{"id": "stub_001", "char_prose": "Kira is a scout of the Ridgewatch company.\nKira is strong-limbed, light-footed, and sharp-eyed.\nKira is cautious, driven, and methodical.\nKira is at full strength, and composed.\nKira carries a shortbow, a quiver of twenty broadheads, a short blade, and a scouting kit.\nShe has fought through forty-seven goblin engagements, twelve beast hunts, and three skirmishes with undead. She has succeeded at stealth approaches eight times and failed three and succeeded at ridge traversals four times and failed zero. She has spent eighty hours scouting and twelve hours at the forge. She knows ridge terrain well, forest terrain moderately, and dungeon corridors barely.\nKira's defining moments include: her first kill, a goblin scout in the Hollowwood; crossing the Ashridge under fire with the whole company watching; surviving three days alone after the Coldmere ambush.", "action_prose": "The action is a stealth approach on loose scree.\nThe target is a goblin sentry post on a rocky ridge.\nThe approach requires moving without sound across unstable ground.\nThe operative crosses open ground in fading light.\nPartial cover is available from scattered boulders.\nThe terrain is loose scree, requiring careful footwork.\nThe operative must close to within thirty feet without alerting the sentries.\nSuccess produces a flanking advantage; failure triggers an alarm.", "context_prose": "The scene is a contested ridge under a moonless sky.\nThe weather is clear but cold, with a light wind from the north.\nThe time is deep night, two hours before dawn.\nVisibility is poor beyond thirty feet.\nThe ground is loose scree on a fifteen-degree slope.\nThe Ridgewatch company is positioned two hundred feet to the south, awaiting the scout's signal.\nThree goblin sentries hold the crest; one is drowsy.", "expected_delta": 4.5, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Kira has 8 stealth-approach successes and 4 ridge traversals. Terrain is ridge scree -- her best-known terrain. Night ops favor the scout. Strong positive delta."}
{"id": "stub_002", "char_prose": "Kira is a scout of the Ridgewatch company.\nKira is strong-limbed, light-footed, and sharp-eyed.\nKira is cautious, driven, and methodical.\nKira is at full strength, and composed.\nKira carries a shortbow, a quiver of twenty broadheads, a short blade, and a scouting kit.\nShe has fought through forty-seven goblin engagements, twelve beast hunts, and three skirmishes with undead. She has succeeded at stealth approaches eight times and failed three and succeeded at ridge traversals four times and failed zero. She has spent eighty hours scouting and twelve hours at the forge. She knows ridge terrain well, forest terrain moderately, and dungeon corridors barely.\nKira's defining moments include: her first kill, a goblin scout in the Hollowwood; crossing the Ashridge under fire with the whole company watching; surviving three days alone after the Coldmere ambush.", "action_prose": "The action is a direct assault on a fortified position.\nThe target is a stone gatehouse held by twelve armed guards.\nThe operative charges the main gate without cover.\nThe approach is across open ground in full daylight.\nNo cover is available between the tree line and the gate.\nThe terrain is flat cobblestone, offering no advantage to a scout.\nThe operative must reach the gate and break through under sustained fire.\nSuccess secures the gatehouse; failure results in the operative being cut down.", "context_prose": "The scene is a fortified town gate in full daylight.\nThe weather is clear, with excellent visibility.\nThe time is midday.\nTwelve armored guards hold the gatehouse.\nThe open ground is eighty feet across.\nNo allied forces are in position to provide covering fire.", "expected_delta": -3.5, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Kira is a scout, not a heavy assault specialist. No matching legacy for frontal assaults. Terrain is flat cobblestone -- not her domain. Strong negative."}
{"id": "stub_003", "char_prose": "Brennan is a fighter of the Ironwall garrison.\nBrennan is powerfully built, slow-footed, and keen-minded.\nBrennan is bold and stubborn.\nBrennan is slightly wounded, with a gash on his left forearm, and steady.\nBrennan carries a tower shield, a longsword, and chainmail.\nHe has fought through thirty heavy infantry engagements and five siege actions. He has succeeded at holding the line twelve times and failed two and succeeded at shield wall formations eight times and failed one. He has spent two hundred hours in garrison duty and sixty hours drilling formations. He knows open battlefield terrain well and fortress corridors moderately.", "action_prose": "The action is holding a narrow chokepoint against a surge of undead.\nThe target position is a doorway three feet wide in a dungeon corridor.\nThe fighter plants the shield and holds ground as waves of undead press forward.\nThe corridor limits the number of attackers to two abreast.\nThe fighter must not be pushed back for sixty seconds.\nSuccess holds the line for the party to escape; failure breaks the formation.", "context_prose": "The scene is a dungeon corridor, twenty feet long and eight feet wide.\nThe time is unknown -- no light enters from outside.\nThe walls are damp stone.\nFour party members are retreating behind the fighter.\nUndead number approximately thirty, pressing from the north end of the corridor.\nThe fighter has held such positions twice before in this dungeon.", "expected_delta": 3.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Brennan has 12 hold-the-line successes and 8 shield wall successes. Chokepoint plays to his kit. Dungeon corridors are moderate for him. Good positive delta; not maximum because terrain is not his best."}
{"id": "stub_004", "char_prose": "Mira is an arcanist of the Pale Tower.\nMira is frail, deft-fingered, and deeply perceptive.\nMira is curious and meticulous.\nMira is at full strength, and untroubled.\nMira carries a spell focus, a leather satchel of reagents, and a walking staff.\nShe has succeeded at arcane rituals fourteen times and failed one and succeeded at translating ancient scripts nine times and failed two. She has spent three hundred hours in arcane study and forty hours at the observatory. She knows the Pale Tower grounds best of all and the market district barely.", "action_prose": "The action is translating a partially-damaged glyph sequence on a dungeon wall.\nThe glyphs are written in an archaic dialect of High Valdric.\nThe arcanist must reconstruct the missing portions from context and grammatical rules.\nA successful translation reveals the location of a hidden vault.\nThe work requires stillness and concentration for approximately ten minutes.\nThe dungeon is quiet; no immediate threat is present.", "context_prose": "The scene is a dusty archive chamber deep in the dungeon.\nThe time is uncertain; no light enters from outside.\nThe chamber is dry and undisturbed.\nA single torch provides adequate illumination.\nNo combat is ongoing.\nThe party has thirty minutes before the patrol circuit returns.", "expected_delta": 3.5, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Mira has 9 successful script translations. The task is squarely in her domain. Quiet environment is ideal. Moderate positive delta (high confidence but not maximum -- partial glyph damage adds difficulty)."}
{"id": "stub_005", "char_prose": "Brennan is a fighter of the Ironwall garrison.\nBrennan is powerfully built, slow-footed, and keen-minded.\nBrennan is bold and stubborn.\nBrennan is exhausted, and strained from three days without sleep.\nBrennan carries a tower shield, a longsword, and chainmail.\nHe has fought through thirty heavy infantry engagements and five siege actions. He has succeeded at holding the line twelve times and failed two and succeeded at shield wall formations eight times and failed one. He has spent two hundred hours in garrison duty and sixty hours drilling formations. He knows open battlefield terrain well and fortress corridors moderately.", "action_prose": "The action is a forced march across forty miles of open highland in a single day.\nThe party must reach the garrison before the enemy column cuts off the road.\nBrennan must set the pace for the group while wearing full plate armor.\nThe march requires sustained physical output over twelve hours.\nNo combat is expected, but the pace cannot slacken.\nSuccess delivers the party to the garrison before the road is cut.", "context_prose": "The scene is open highland, rolling hills, moderate trail.\nThe weather is overcast and mild, with light rain expected in the afternoon.\nThe time is early morning; the party has twelve hours of daylight.\nBrennan has not slept in three days.\nThe enemy column was last spotted fifteen miles to the east, moving north.", "expected_delta": -2.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Brennan has no march-endurance legacy. He is exhausted. Plate armor on a 40-mile march punishes him. Moderate negative; not extreme because the terrain is open field (his domain) and the march is achievable at a cost."}
{"id": "stub_006", "char_prose": "Lyra is a healer of the Amber Order.\nLyra is slight, steady-handed, and wise.\nLyra is compassionate and patient.\nLyra is at full strength, and serene.\nLyra carries a healer's kit, a belt of vials, and a quarterstaff.\nShe has succeeded at field surgery eighteen times and failed two and succeeded at diagnosing poison twelve times and failed one. She has spent four hundred hours in the infirmary and twenty hours on patrol. She knows the infirmary and the Amber Order grounds best of all and wilderness terrain barely.", "action_prose": "The action is treating a deep stab wound in the field.\nThe patient is a companion with a blade lodged between the fourth and fifth rib.\nThe healer must remove the blade, pack the wound, and stabilize the patient for transport.\nThe procedure requires clean hands, adequate light, and minimal patient movement.\nSuccess stabilizes the patient; failure risks collapse within the hour.", "context_prose": "The scene is a forest clearing, thirty feet across.\nThe time is dusk; light is fading.\nThe ground is damp but level.\nNo combat is ongoing.\nThe healer has a fire for sterilization and a lantern for light.\nThe patient is conscious and cooperative.", "expected_delta": 3.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Lyra has 18 field surgery successes. The action is her core competency. Conditions are suboptimal (field, fading light) but not terrible. Good positive delta."}
{"id": "stub_007", "char_prose": "Kira is a scout of the Ridgewatch company.\nKira is strong-limbed, light-footed, and sharp-eyed.\nKira is cautious and driven.\nKira is badly wounded, with a arrow in her left shoulder, and rattled from a close call.\nKira carries a shortbow, a quiver of eight broadheads, a short blade, and a scouting kit.\nShe has fought through forty-seven goblin engagements, twelve beast hunts, and three skirmishes with undead. She has succeeded at stealth approaches eight times and failed three. She has spent eighty hours scouting. She knows ridge terrain well and forest terrain moderately.\nKira's defining moments include: her first kill, a goblin scout in the Hollowwood; crossing the Ashridge under fire.", "action_prose": "The action is a stealth approach on loose scree.\nThe target is a goblin sentry post on a rocky ridge.\nThe approach requires moving without sound across unstable ground.\nThe operative must close to within thirty feet without alerting the sentries.\nThe operative has a significant shoulder injury that limits arm movement.\nSuccess produces a flanking advantage; failure triggers an alarm.", "context_prose": "The scene is a contested ridge under a moonless sky.\nThe weather is clear but cold.\nThe time is deep night.\nThe ground is loose scree.\nKira's left shoulder is immobilized from the arrow wound.", "expected_delta": 1.5, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Same scenario as stub_001 but Kira is badly wounded and rattled. Legacy advantage is still present but physical penalty is significant. Moderate positive -- legacy pulls up, injury pulls down."}
{"id": "stub_008", "char_prose": "Torval is a young recruit of the Ridgewatch company.\nTorval is average-built, clumsy, and inexperienced.\nTorval is eager but nervous.\nTorval is at full strength, but anxious.\nTorval carries a short sword and a dented buckler.\nHe has no recorded engagements. He has no recorded action successes. He has spent two weeks in basic training. He knows the company camp barely.", "action_prose": "The action is a stealth approach on loose scree.\nThe target is a goblin sentry post on a rocky ridge.\nThe approach requires moving without sound across unstable ground.\nThe operative must close to within thirty feet without alerting the sentries.\nSuccess produces a flanking advantage; failure triggers an alarm.", "context_prose": "The scene is a contested ridge under a moonless sky.\nThe weather is clear but cold.\nThe time is deep night.\nThe ground is loose scree.", "expected_delta": -2.5, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Same action as stub_001 but Torval has zero relevant legacy and is anxious. Negative delta: no training, unfamiliar terrain, no stealth history."}
{"id": "stub_009", "char_prose": "Mira is an arcanist of the Pale Tower.\nMira is frail, deft-fingered, and deeply perceptive.\nMira is curious and meticulous.\nMira is at full strength, and untroubled.\nMira carries a spell focus, a leather satchel of reagents, and a walking staff.\nShe has succeeded at arcane rituals fourteen times and failed one. She has spent three hundred hours in arcane study.", "action_prose": "The action is a direct assault on a fortified position.\nThe target is a stone gatehouse held by twelve armed guards.\nThe operative charges the main gate without cover.\nThe approach is across open ground in full daylight.\nNo cover is available.\nThe operative must reach the gate and break through under sustained fire.", "context_prose": "The scene is a fortified town gate in full daylight.\nTwelve armored guards hold the gatehouse.\nNo allied forces are in position to provide covering fire.", "expected_delta": -4.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Mira has zero combat legacy and is frail. Frontal assault is completely outside her competency. Strong negative delta."}
{"id": "stub_010", "char_prose": "Wren is a rogue of the Twilight Guild.\nWren is wiry, quick-footed, and perceptive.\nWren is cunning and adaptable.\nWren is at full strength, and calm.\nWren carries a pair of daggers, thieves' tools, and a dark cloak.\nShe has succeeded at lockpicking twenty-two times and failed three and succeeded at pickpocketing fifteen times and failed four and succeeded at social deception eleven times and failed two. She has spent one hundred fifty hours on guild contracts and thirty hours in disguise work. She knows the market district best of all, the docks moderately, and the noble quarter barely.", "action_prose": "The action is picking a complex lock on a merchant vault.\nThe vault is secured with a triple-tumbler mechanism of Dwarven make.\nThe rogue must feel the mechanism and manipulate each tumbler in sequence.\nThe work requires a quiet environment, steady hands, and at least three minutes.\nA successful pick opens the vault without triggering the alarm.\nA failure triggers the alarm and alerts the guards.", "context_prose": "The scene is a back room in a wealthy merchant's warehouse.\nThe time is past midnight.\nThe guards are on a thirty-minute patrol circuit; the rogue has twelve minutes.\nThe room is quiet and dimly lit by a single lantern left by the guards.\nNo other party members are present.", "expected_delta": 4.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Wren has 22 lockpick successes. Triple-tumbler is hard but this is her primary skill. Quiet environment, adequate time, correct tools. Strong positive."}
{"id": "stub_011", "char_prose": "Wren is a rogue of the Twilight Guild.\nWren is wiry, quick-footed, and perceptive.\nWren is cunning and adaptable.\nWren is at full strength, and calm.\nWren carries a pair of daggers, thieves' tools, and a dark cloak.\nShe has succeeded at lockpicking twenty-two times and failed three and succeeded at social deception eleven times and failed two. She knows the market district best of all and the noble quarter barely.", "action_prose": "The action is negotiating trade terms with a merchant guild representative.\nThe operative must convince the representative to accept below-market prices for a shipment.\nThe negotiation requires knowledge of commercial law and pricing conventions.\nThe operative must not reveal that the party is working against the guild's interests.\nSuccess secures the shipment at favorable terms; failure alerts the guild to the party's agenda.", "context_prose": "The scene is a guild meeting hall in the noble quarter.\nThe time is midday; the hall is busy with other merchants.\nThe representative is experienced and suspicious of newcomers.\nWren is wearing a disguise as a Valdric merchant.", "expected_delta": 1.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Wren has social deception legacy (11 successes) but no commercial negotiation history. Disguise is in her kit but the noble quarter is unfamiliar. Moderate positive -- deception skill carries partially, but wrong context reduces it."}
{"id": "stub_012", "char_prose": "Brennan is a fighter of the Ironwall garrison.\nBrennan is powerfully built, slow-footed, and keen-minded.\nBrennan is bold and stubborn.\nBrennan is at full strength, and steady.\nBrennan carries a tower shield, a longsword, and chainmail.\nHe has fought through thirty heavy infantry engagements and five siege actions. He has succeeded at holding the line twelve times and failed two. He knows open battlefield terrain well and fortress corridors moderately.", "action_prose": "The action is a shield wall formation with two allied fighters.\nThree fighters must lock shields and advance twenty feet across open ground against a cavalry charge.\nTiming must be precise -- the wall must hold until the cavalry breaks on the shields.\nSuccess stops the charge and creates an opening for a counterattack.\nFailure breaks the line and exposes the rear formations.", "context_prose": "The scene is an open battlefield, flat ground, midday.\nA cavalry unit of eight riders is charging from the north at full gallop.\nTwo allied fighters are in position on Brennan's flanks.\nThe allied fighters are experienced -- they have held shield walls before.\nThe ground is firm and level.", "expected_delta": 4.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Brennan has 8 shield wall successes and 12 hold-the-line successes. Open battlefield is his best terrain. Allied fighters are experienced. Strong positive delta."}
{"id": "stub_013", "char_prose": "Lyra is a healer of the Amber Order.\nLyra is slight, steady-handed, and wise.\nLyra is compassionate and patient.\nLyra is at full strength, and serene.\nLyra carries a healer's kit, a belt of vials, and a quarterstaff.\nShe has succeeded at field surgery eighteen times and failed two and succeeded at diagnosing poison twelve times and failed one. She has spent four hundred hours in the infirmary.", "action_prose": "The action is identifying and treating an unknown magical disease.\nThe patient is displaying symptoms that match no known mundane ailment.\nThe healer must diagnose from symptoms alone, without reference materials.\nThe disease may be of arcane origin, requiring both medical and arcane knowledge.\nA wrong treatment could accelerate the progression.\nSuccess stabilizes the patient; failure causes rapid deterioration.", "context_prose": "The scene is a field camp, twenty miles from the nearest settlement.\nNo arcane resources are available.\nThe patient has been symptomatic for six hours.\nA healer's kit is available but no specialized equipment.\nThe time is evening; a fire provides warmth and light.", "expected_delta": -1.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Lyra has strong mundane healing legacy but no arcane diagnosis experience. Magical disease is outside her documented competency. Slight negative -- her base skill partially applies but the arcane component is a gap."}
{"id": "stub_014", "char_prose": "Torval is a young recruit of the Ridgewatch company.\nTorval is average-built, clumsy, and inexperienced.\nTorval is eager but nervous.\nTorval is at full strength, but anxious.\nTorval carries a short sword and a dented buckler.\nHe has no recorded engagements. He has no recorded action successes. He has spent two weeks in basic training. He knows the company camp barely.", "action_prose": "The action is carrying a message from the camp to the forward post.\nThe messenger must travel one mile along a marked trail in daylight.\nNo enemy contact is expected on the route.\nThe message must arrive intact and unread.\nSuccess delivers the message on time.", "context_prose": "The scene is a forest trail between the main camp and the forward post.\nThe time is midday.\nThe trail is well-marked and lightly used.\nNo enemy forces have been reported in the area.\nThe distance is one mile on flat terrain.", "expected_delta": 0.5, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Low-difficulty task matching Torval's capability level. No legacy required; the action is within baseline human competency. Slight positive -- easy task, no mismatch penalty."}
{"id": "stub_015", "char_prose": "Kira is a scout of the Ridgewatch company.\nKira is strong-limbed, light-footed, and sharp-eyed.\nKira is cautious, driven, and methodical.\nKira is at full strength, and composed.\nKira carries a shortbow, a quiver of twenty broadheads, a short blade, and a scouting kit.\nShe has fought through forty-seven goblin engagements, twelve beast hunts, and three skirmishes with undead. She has succeeded at stealth approaches eight times and failed three and succeeded at ridge traversals four times and failed zero. She has spent eighty hours scouting. She knows ridge terrain well and forest terrain moderately.", "action_prose": "The action is long-range archery at a moving target.\nThe target is a goblin warg-rider moving at speed across open ground at one hundred fifty feet.\nThe operative must lead the shot and account for the warg's gait.\nThe wind is moderate and crosswise to the shot.\nOne arrow available before the target passes out of range.\nSuccess drops the warg-rider before it reaches the column.", "context_prose": "The scene is an open ridge, late afternoon.\nThe wind is blowing at fifteen miles per hour from the west.\nThe target is moving north at a canter, crossing left to right at one hundred fifty feet.\nNo allied forces are in the shot path.\nThe light is adequate but the sun is low in the west.", "expected_delta": 2.0, "grader_id": "tess", "notes": "Kira has ranged combat legacy (47 goblin engagements) but no specific archery-at-moving-target record. Ridge terrain is her domain. Moderate positive -- general combat experience applies, specific moving-target experience is missing."}
